From e1e7837e7436c41b20e07a225a428ca64597cbb0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 22:02:20 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 083/102] render: camera paths, camerafade and the transparent
 sort's sortorder
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`camera.paths` names a camera paths file (GH 0x1401c6ef0: paths[] of {duration, disabled,
transforms[] of {eye, center, up, zoom = 1, timestamp (else i / (n − 1) · duration), disabled}};
the loader GH 0x1401b6c60 reads each string entry into the same list, so the last wins). The
camera update GH 0x1401b8af0 plays them while no camera object is active: a key holds before its
time; between two keys a cubic Hermite with both tangents (b − a) / 2; the path index wraps.
A 3D scene takes the eye, centre and up; a 2D scene the key's zoom (in place of general.zoom)
and the eye's offset from the scene camera's. camerafade (general flag 4) draws
materials/util/fade.json over the scene (GH 0x1401afbf0): alpha 1 − 2 · remaining over a
path's last 0.5 s, 1 − 2 · t over its first; its colour the `schemecolor` property · 0.7
(fade.frag; the binding inferred from usershadervalues).

transparentsorting's key is WE's (GH 0x1401b6660, stable sort, comparator GH 0x1401cc550):
the objects' `sortorder` (base object int +0x124) ascending, then farthest first along the
view direction. LWE sorted by the distance from the eye and ignored sortorder.

Origin: ours
Why: docs/player/spikes/we-coverage.md F5 (G23 camerafade, camera paths, sortorder)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
